                    "id": "discrete-dist",
                    "label": "Standard Discrete Distributions",
                    "content": "## Standard Discrete Distributions\n\n### Master Reference Table\n\n| Distribution | PMF \\(P(X=x)\\) | Mean | Variance | Median | Mode | MGF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Uniform\\(\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\) | \\(1/N\\) | \\((N+1)/2\\) | \\((N^2-1)/12\\) | \\((N+1)/2\\) | Every value | \\(\\dfrac{e^t(1-e^{Nt})}{N(1-e^t)}\\) |\n| Bernoulli\\((p)\\) | \\(p^x q^{1-x}\\), \\(x=0,1\\) | \\(p\\) | \\(pq\\) | \\(0\\) if \\(p<\\tfrac{1}{2}\\); \\(1\\) if \\(p>\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) | \\(0\\) if \\(p<\\tfrac{1}{2}\\); \\(1\\) if \\(p>\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) | \\(q+pe^t\\) |\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\(\\binom{n}{x}p^x q^{n-x}\\) | \\(np\\) | \\(npq\\) | \\(\\lfloor np \\rfloor\\) or \\(\\lceil np \\rceil\\) | \\(\\lfloor (n+1)p \\rfloor\\) | \\((q+pe^t)^n\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^x/x!\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(\\approx\\lfloor\\lambda+\\tfrac{1}{3}\\rfloor\\) | \\(\\lfloor\\lambda\\rfloor\\) (two modes if \\(\\lambda\\in\\mathbb{Z}\\)) | \\(e^{\\lambda(e^t-1)}\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(q^x p\\), \\(x=0,1,2,\\ldots\\) | \\(q/p\\) | \\(q/p^2\\) | \\(\\left\\lceil\\tfrac{-1}{\\ln q}\\right\\rceil-1\\) | \\(0\\) | \\(p(1-qe^t)^{-1}\\) |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\(\\binom{x+r-1}{x}p^r q^x\\) | \\(rq/p\\) | \\(rq/p^2\\) | \\(\\approx\\lfloor rq/p\\rfloor\\) | \\(\\lfloor(r-1)q/p\\rfloor\\) for \\(r>1\\); \\(0\\) for \\(r=1\\) | \\((p/(1-qe^t))^r\\) |\n| Hypergeometric | \\(\\dfrac{\\binom{M}{x}\\binom{N-M}{n-x}}{\\binom{N}{n}}\\) | \\(nM/N\\) | \\(n\\dfrac{M}{N}\\dfrac{N-M}{N}\\dfrac{N-n}{N-1}\\) | — | \\(\\left\\lfloor\\dfrac{(M+1)(n+1)}{N+2}\\right\\rfloor\\) | — |\n| Multinomial | \\(\\dfrac{n!}{x_1!\\cdots x_k!}p_1^{x_1}\\cdots p_k^{x_k}\\) | \\(np_i\\) | \\(np_iq_i\\) | — | — | \\(\\left(\\sum p_i e^{t_i}\\right)^n\\) |\n\n---\n\n### Skewness, Kurtosis & Shape\n\n| Distribution | \\(\\gamma_1\\) (Skewness) | Direction | \\(\\beta_2\\) (Kurtosis) | Shape |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Uniform Discrete | \\(0\\) | Symmetric | \\(\\dfrac{3(N^2+1)}{5(N^2-1)}\\cdot\\dfrac{N^2-1}{1}<3\\) | **Platykurtic** |\n| Bernoulli\\((p)\\) | \\(\\dfrac{q-p}{\\sqrt{pq}}\\) | Right if \\(p<\\tfrac{1}{2}\\); Left if \\(p>\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) | \\(3+\\dfrac{1-6pq}{pq}\\) | **Platykurtic** (\\(\\beta_2<3\\)) |\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\(\\dfrac{q-p}{\\sqrt{npq}}\\) | Right if \\(p<\\tfrac{1}{2}\\); Left if \\(p>\\tfrac{1}{2}\\); 0 if \\(p=\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) | \\(3+\\dfrac{1-6pq}{npq}\\) | Approaches Normal as \\(n\\to\\infty\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(1/\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\) | Always **right-skewed** | \\(3+1/\\lambda\\) | Always **leptokurtic**; \\(\\to\\) Normal as \\(\\lambda\\to\\infty\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(\\dfrac{2-p}{\\sqrt{q}}\\) | Always **right-skewed** | \\(3+\\dfrac{p^2+6q}{q}\\) | Always **leptokurtic** |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\(\\dfrac{2-p}{\\sqrt{rq}}\\) | Always **right-skewed** | \\(3+\\dfrac{6}{r}+\\dfrac{p^2}{rq}\\) | Always **leptokurtic**; \\(\\to\\) Normal as \\(r\\to\\infty\\) |\n| Hypergeometric | \\(\\dfrac{(N-2M)\\sqrt{N-1}\\cdot\\sqrt{N}}{\\sqrt{nM(N-M)(N-n)}}\\) | Right if \\(M < N/2\\); Left if \\(M > N/2\\); Symmetric if \\(M = N/2\\) | Complex expression | Approaches Normal for large \\(n, N\\) |\n---\n\n### PGFs\n\n| Distribution | PGF \\(G(s) = E(s^X)\\) |\n|---|---|\n| Uniform\\(\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\) | \\(\\dfrac{s(1-s^N)}{N(1-s)}\\) |\n| Bernoulli\\((p)\\) | \\(q + ps\\) |\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\((q+ps)^n\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(e^{\\lambda(s-1)}\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(p/(1-qs)\\) |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\((p/(1-qs))^r\\) |\n\n*Recall: \\(P(X=k) = G^{(k)}(0)/k!\\); \\(E(X) = G'(1)\\); \\(E[X(X-1)] = G''(1)\\)*\n\n---\n\n### Cumulants\n\n| Distribution | \\(\\kappa_1\\) (Mean) | \\(\\kappa_2\\) (Variance) | All cumulants \\(\\kappa_r\\) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\(np\\) | \\(npq\\) | Via CGF \\(n\\ln(q+pe^t)\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(\\kappa_r = \\lambda\\) for **all** \\(r\\ge1\\) — **unique property** |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\(rq/p\\) | \\(rq/p^2\\) | Via CGF \\(r\\ln\\tfrac{p}{1-qe^t}\\) |\n\n---\n\n### Dispersion: Mean vs Variance\n\n| Distribution | Relationship | Type |\n|---|---|---|\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | Mean \\(> \\) Var \\((q < 1)\\) | **Underdispersed** |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | Mean \\(= \\) Var \\(= \\lambda\\) | **Equidispersed** |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | Mean \\(< \\) Var \\((1/p > 1)\\) | **Overdispersed** |\n\n*Index of dispersion \\(= \\sigma^2/\\mu\\): \\(<1\\) underdispersed, \\(=1\\) Poisson, \\(>1\\) overdispersed*\n\n---\n\n### Key Properties & Relationships\n\n- **Discrete Uniform variance:** \\((N^2-1)/12\\) where \\(N\\) = number of values — analogue of continuous Uniform \\((b-a)^2/12\\)\n- **Bernoulli variance** maximised at \\(p=1/2\\) (\\(pq\\) max \\(= 1/4\\)); \\(\\text{Bernoulli}(p) = B(1,p)\\)\n- **Binomial skew direction:** \\(p<1/2\\) \\(\\Rightarrow\\) right-skewed; \\(p>1/2\\) \\(\\Rightarrow\\) left-skewed; \\(p=1/2\\) \\(\\Rightarrow\\) symmetric\n- **Binomial mode:** \\(\\lfloor(n+1)p\\rfloor\\); if \\((n+1)p\\) is an integer, **two modes** at \\((n+1)p\\) and \\((n+1)p-1\\)\n- **Binomial reproductive:** \\(X_i\\sim B(n_i,p)\\) independent \\(\\Rightarrow \\sum X_i \\sim B(\\sum n_i, p)\\)\n- **Poisson as limit of Binomial:** \\(B(n,p)\\to\\text{Poisson}(\\lambda)\\) as \\(n\\to\\infty\\), \\(p\\to 0\\), \\(np\\to\\lambda\\)\n- **Poisson cumulants:** ALL cumulants \\(= \\lambda\\) — unique property; mean \\(=\\) variance \\(=\\) skewness-numerator \\(=\\lambda\\)\n- **Poisson reproductive:** \\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda_1)\\), \\(Y\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda_2)\\) independent \\(\\Rightarrow X+Y\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2)\\)\n- **Geometric memoryless:** \\(P(X>m+n\\mid X>m) = P(X>n)\\) — only discrete memoryless distribution\n- **Geometric mode always 0** (number-of-failures parameterisation); always right-skewed, leptokurtic\n- **NegBin = sum of \\(r\\) independent Geometric RVs:** \\(\\text{NegBin}(1,p) = \\text{Geometric}(p)\\)\n- **NegBin always overdispersed:** Var \\(= rq/p^2 >\\) Mean \\(= rq/p\\) since \\(1/p > 1\\)\n- **Hypergeometric \\(\\to\\) Binomial** when \\(N\\to\\infty\\), \\(M/N\\to p\\); FPC factor \\((N-n)/(N-1)\\to 1\\)\n- **Hypergeometric covariance:** \\(\\text{Cov}(X_i,X_j) = -\\frac{np_ip_j}{N-1} < 0\\) (negative — sampling without replacement)\n- **Multinomial marginals** are Binomial: \\(X_i\\sim B(n,p_i)\\)\n- **Multinomial covariance:** \\(\\text{Cov}(X_i,X_j) = -np_ip_j < 0\\) for \\(i\\ne j\\) — always negative\n- **Poisson \\(\\to\\) Normal:** As \\(\\lambda\\to\\infty\\), \\(\\frac{X-\\lambda}{\\sqrt{\\lambda}}\\xrightarrow{d}N(0,1)\\)\n\n> **ISS tip:** Discrete Uniform variance = \\((N^2-1)/12\\). Poisson is the **only** distribution where all cumulants equal \\(\\lambda\\); mean = variance — index of dispersion = 1. Geometric mode = **0** always. Binomial: \\(p<1/2\\) right-skewed, \\(p>1/2\\) left-skewed. NegBin is always overdispersed (variance > mean); used when Poisson equidispersion fails. Fisher's Ideal index satisfies both TRT and FRT. Hypergeometric FPC \\((N-n)/(N-1)\\): as \\(N\\to\\infty\\), FPC\\(\\to 1\\) and distribution \\(\\to\\) Binomial. Multinomial covariance between components is always **negative**.\n"
