                    "content": "## Hardware — Input, Output & Peripheral Devices\n\n### Input Devices\n\n| Device | Type of Input |\n|---|---|\n| Keyboard | Text / commands |\n| Mouse | Pointing / clicking |\n| Scanner | Image / document digitisation |\n| Microphone | Audio |\n| Webcam | Video / image |\n| Barcode reader | Product codes |\n| OMR (Optical Mark Reader) | Marks on paper (MCQ sheets) |\n| OCR (Optical Character Reader) | Printed text recognition |\n| Touchscreen | Touch input |\n\n### Output Devices\n\n| Device | Output Type |\n|---|---|\n| Monitor (CRT, LCD, LED) | Visual display |\n| Printer (Inkjet, Laser, Dot-matrix) | Hard copy |\n| Plotter | Large-scale diagrams / CAD |\n| Speaker | Audio |\n| Projector | Magnified display |\n\n### Secondary Storage Devices\n\n| Device | Technology | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HDD (Hard Disk Drive) | Magnetic | High capacity; slower |\n| SSD (Solid State Drive) | Flash memory | Fast; no moving parts |\n| CD / DVD | Optical | CD: 700 MB; DVD: 4.7 GB |\n| Blu-ray | Optical | 25–50 GB |\n| USB Flash Drive | Flash | Portable |\n| Magnetic Tape | Magnetic | Backup; sequential access |\n\n### Bus Types\n\n- **Data Bus** — carries actual data (bidirectional)\n- **Address Bus** — carries memory addresses (unidirectional)\n- **Control Bus** — carries control signals\n\n### Ports & Interfaces\n\n| Port | Use |\n|---|---|\n| USB (Universal Serial Bus) | Most peripherals |\n| HDMI | Video/audio to display |\n| Ethernet (RJ-45) | Wired network |\n| Wi-Fi | Wireless network |\n| Bluetooth | Short-range wireless |\n\n> **ISS tip:** OMR is specifically used for MCQ answer sheets — very ISS-relevant context. Know the difference between input/output/storage devices. Printer types: inkjet (home), laser (office), dot-matrix (carbon copies)."
