            "tips": "**High-priority topics for ISS Official Statistics section (Paper II):**\n\n**Institutional knowledge (most-tested):**\n- **NSO formed 23 May 2019** = merger of NSSO + CSO; under MoSPI; headed by Secretary (Statistics & PI)\n- **NSSO established 1950;** 4 divisions: SDRD (Kolkata), FOD, DPD (Kolkata/Faridabad), CPD\n- **NSC constituted 12 July 2006** — by executive resolution (NOT Act of Parliament) — Rangarajan Commission recommendation (2001)\n- NSC: 1 Chairperson + 4 Members + 1 ex-officio; CSI = Secretary to NSC\n- NSC members removed only by **President** after Supreme Court inquiry\n- **RGI** under Ministry of **Home Affairs** (not MoSPI) — conducts Population Census and CRS\n\n**Key legislation:**\n- **Collection of Statistics Act, 2008** — primary legislation for data collection\n- **Census Act, 1948** — Population Census legal basis\n- **Registration of Births and Deaths Act, 1969** — CRS legal basis\n- **ISI Act, 1959** — ISI Kolkata as Institute of National Importance\n\n**Index numbers (most-tested):**\n- **Fisher's Ideal Index:** Satisfies BOTH Time Reversal Test AND Factor Reversal Test — only index to do so\n- **WPI:** Base 2011-12; compiled by **OEA/DPIIT** (Ministry of Commerce); measures wholesale prices; monthly (14th)\n- **CPI (Combined):** Base 2012=100; compiled by **MoSPI**; headline inflation indicator; Food weight ~45.86%\n- **CPI-IW:** Base 2016=100; compiled by **Labour Bureau** (Ministry of Labour) — used for DA calculation\n- **IIP:** Base 2011-12; compiled by **NSO/MoSPI**; monthly (28th of next month + 6 weeks)\n- New GDP base year (released 27 Feb 2026): **2022-23** (9th series; replaced 2011-12)\n\n**National Accounts:**\n- GDP (Market Price) = GVA (Basic Prices) + Net Taxes on Products\n- GNP = GDP + NFIA; NNP = GNP − Depreciation; NI = NNP at Factor Cost\n- GDP Deflator = Nominal GDP / Real GDP × 100\n- India follows **SNA 2008**; plans to shift to SNA 2025 in next revision\n- GDP release: AE (Jan) → SAE (Feb 28) → PE (May 31) → FRE (following Jan)\n\n**Population Census:**\n- Decennial — year ending in **1**; legal basis: **Census Act, 1948**\n- Census 2011: Population **121.09 crore**; Literacy **74.04%**; Sex ratio **943**; Child sex ratio **919**\n- India follows **de jure** (usual residence) method\n- 2021 Census: postponed due to COVID; yet to be conducted\n\n**Key surveys (frequently tested):**\n- **PLFS** (from 2017-18): Annual + quarterly urban; replaces EUS; measures LFPR, WPR, UR by UPSS/CWS/CDS\n- **NFHS:** Conducted by **IIPS Mumbai** (not NSO); NFHS-5 (2019-21); TFR = 2.0\n- **HCES 2022-23:** Household Consumption Expenditure Survey (formerly CES); used for poverty estimation\n- **ASI:** Annual Survey of Industries — organised manufacturing sector; by NSO\n- **Economic Census:** Complete enumeration of all non-agricultural establishments; 7th EC in 2019\n- **Agricultural Census:** Every 5 years — NOT 10 years\n- **SRS:** Sample Registration System by RGI — annual vital rates (birth rate, death rate, IMR, TFR)\n\n**Socio-economic indicators:**\n- **HDI = geometric mean** of Life Expectancy Index × Education Index × GNI Index\n- **Gini coefficient:** 0 = perfect equality; 1 = perfect inequality\n- **CDS** gives highest unemployment rate; UPSS gives lowest — CDS most sensitive to underemployment\n- **SDG India Index:** Published by **NITI Aayog**\n- India is **SDDS subscriber** to IMF — commits to Advance Release Calendar and transparency"
