            "tips": "**Applied Statistics — Final Tips & Exam Strategy:**\n\n1. **Index Numbers — Two guaranteed derivations:** (1) Prove Fisher satisfies TRT: write \\( P_{01}^F \\times P_{10}^F \\), expand both square roots as products of Laspeyres and Paasche, show exact cancellation gives 1. (2) Prove Fisher satisfies FRT: swap \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) to form \\( Q_{01}^F \\), multiply \\( P_{01}^F \\times Q_{01}^F \\), show it equals \\( \\sum p_1q_1/\\sum p_0q_0 \\). Write every summation step — partial proofs lose marks.\n2. **Demand Analysis — Leontief vs Pigou:** State the data source clearly: Leontief uses time-series (estimates price and income elasticity jointly); Pigou uses cross-section family budget data (estimates income elasticity across households at a point in time). This distinction is a direct exam question.\n3. **Trend Determination — All 3 methods:** Know: (1) Least squares — set up and solve normal equations with centred time; (2) Moving averages — state the centring procedure for even \\( k \\) explicitly; (3) Semi-averages — state limitations. For seasonal indices, normalise so they sum to 1200 (monthly) or 400 (quarterly).\n4. **ARIMA identification — The master table:** AR(p): PACF cuts off at \\( p \\), ACF tails off. MA(q): ACF cuts off at \\( q \\), PACF tails off. ARMA(p,q): both tail off. White noise: both near zero for \\( k>0 \\). Write this table in every Box–Jenkins answer. Also state: MA invertibility condition (roots outside unit circle) is needed to write MA as infinite AR.\n5. **Spectral Analysis — Three key facts:** (1) \\( \\int_{-\\pi}^\\pi f(\\omega)d\\omega = \\gamma_0 \\) (total variance = area under spectrum). (2) Raw periodogram is asymptotically unbiased but **inconsistent** — smoothing is necessary. (3) Correlogram and Periodogram are Fourier transform duals (Wiener–Khintchine theorem). State Wold's decomposition theorem to justify existence of MA representation.\n6. **Hawkins–Simon conditions:** Always state both: \\( |I-A| > 0 \\) and all diagonal elements of \\( (I-A) \\) are positive. Give the economic rationale — an industry cannot consume more of its own output than it produces. Practice \\( 3\\times3 \\) matrix inversion for numerical I–O questions.\n7. **NSO base year update (2022-23):** The new GDP base year series (released February 2026) replaced 2011-12. Mention this in national income answers — it shows contemporary awareness which examiners reward."
